		{
			dependencies: ["6416430518B427C3"]
			description: [
				"Artifacts, collectibles and archaeological fragments are called memories with weight because each carries a habit from its former owner. Their powers are conditional, specialised and sometimes awkward."
				"Test relics deliberately and document their effects. A tool that seems weak in ordinary travel may be extraordinary in one biome, structure or machine room."
				"A public museum prevents powerful history from vanishing into forgotten private storage."
				"The Chronicle links mechanics to memory: every portal changes the rules, every structure records a purpose, and every recovered object asks what the settlement will do with its knowledge."
